-- trigger-types: Trigger Types and Variables
DO $do$
DECLARE v_id integer;
BEGIN
  SELECT id INTO v_id FROM "HelpEntry" WHERE keywords[1] = 'trigger-types' ORDER BY id LIMIT 1;
  IF v_id IS NULL THEN
    SELECT id INTO v_id FROM "HelpEntry" WHERE 'trigger-types' = ANY(keywords) ORDER BY id LIMIT 1;
  END IF;
  IF v_id IS NULL THEN
    INSERT INTO "HelpEntry"
      (keywords, title, content, min_level, category, usage, source_file, updated_at)
    VALUES (
      ARRAY['trigger-types', 'trigger types', 'trigger flags', 'flags']::text[],
      'Trigger Types and Variables',
      $help$Flags a trigger can carry, when the server fires them, and what self / actor /
object are. self is always the entity the trigger is attached to.

Fired by the server today:
  LOAD       mob   Mob spawns (boot and respawn). self = actor = the mob.
                   Not fired for mobs made by room:spawn_mobile.
  GREET      mob   A player or mob arrives in the room. self = listener,
  GREET_ALL        actor = arriver. Both flags behave identically.
  SPEECH     mob   Someone uses "say" in the room, or "ask <mob> <topic>".
                   Global speech = the text, lowercased.
                   Via say, actor is the same entity as self (the speaker is
                   not available). Via ask, actor = the asker.
  RECEIVE    mob   A player gives the mob an item. self = mob, actor = giver,
                   object = the item (the only event that sets object).
  COMMAND    mob   A player types any command while in the same room (mob or
                   item triggers; room triggers are not asked). Globals cmd
                   (command word) and args (rest of line). actor = typist.
                   "return false" consumes the command.
  FIGHT      mob   After each combat round while it is a target. self = target,
                   actor = attacker. Throttle with time.stamp.
  ATTACK     mob   A player starts an attack on it. self = target, actor = attacker.
  DEATH      mob   Just before the mob dies. self = actor = the mob.
  GET, DROP, WEAR, REMOVE, USE, CONSUME   object
                   self = the item, actor = the player. object is nil.
  PREENTRY   room  Before movers enter. self = the room, actor = mover.
  POSTENTRY  room  After the mover arrives and GREET ran. Same bindings.

Flag-less: run_room_trigger(zone, id) runs ALL triggers on that room whatever
their flags (self = room). The firetrig command and /api/admin/triggers/fire
also run a body directly.

Also fired: SPEECH_TO (ask/tell/whisper), RANDOM (13 s pulse; GLOBAL lifts the
"zone has players" gate), BRIBE (coins given to a mob; globals value, platinum,
gold, silver, copper; the trigger's num arg is the minimum in copper), HIT_PERCENT
(num arg = HP% threshold), LOOK, GIVE, CAST, LEAVE, ENTRY, DEFEND and object
ATTACK. For RANDOM and HIT_PERCENT the first statement of the body must be the
`if not percent_chance(N) then return true end` gate; the server reads N from it.

NOT fired (no dispatcher): ACT, RESET, TIME, TIMER, AUTO, MEMORY, DOOR. Use wait()
loops started from LOAD, or run_room_trigger, for periodic behaviour.

Full reference (fire order, bindings, API, require, errors):
fierymud-rs/docs/SCRIPTING.md.

Listeners for GREET, SPEECH, COMMAND are things located in the same room that
have triggers (mobs, and items lying on the floor).

Return value: only COMMAND looks at it. "return false" stops the typed
command; anything else lets it continue.$help$,
      100,
      'building',
      'see also: tstat <zone> <id>',
      'data/help/trigger-types.md',
      now()
    );
  ELSE
    UPDATE "HelpEntry" SET
      keywords = ARRAY['trigger-types', 'trigger types', 'trigger flags', 'flags']::text[],
      title = 'Trigger Types and Variables',
      content = $help$Flags a trigger can carry, when the server fires them, and what self / actor /
object are. self is always the entity the trigger is attached to.

Fired by the server today:
  LOAD       mob   Mob spawns (boot and respawn). self = actor = the mob.
                   Not fired for mobs made by room:spawn_mobile.
  GREET      mob   A player or mob arrives in the room. self = listener,
  GREET_ALL        actor = arriver. Both flags behave identically.
  SPEECH     mob   Someone uses "say" in the room, or "ask <mob> <topic>".
                   Global speech = the text, lowercased.
                   Via say, actor is the same entity as self (the speaker is
                   not available). Via ask, actor = the asker.
  RECEIVE    mob   A player gives the mob an item. self = mob, actor = giver,
                   object = the item (the only event that sets object).
  COMMAND    mob   A player types any command while in the same room (mob or
                   item triggers; room triggers are not asked). Globals cmd
                   (command word) and args (rest of line). actor = typist.
                   "return false" consumes the command.
  FIGHT      mob   After each combat round while it is a target. self = target,
                   actor = attacker. Throttle with time.stamp.
  ATTACK     mob   A player starts an attack on it. self = target, actor = attacker.
  DEATH      mob   Just before the mob dies. self = actor = the mob.
  GET, DROP, WEAR, REMOVE, USE, CONSUME   object
                   self = the item, actor = the player. object is nil.
  PREENTRY   room  Before movers enter. self = the room, actor = mover.
  POSTENTRY  room  After the mover arrives and GREET ran. Same bindings.

Flag-less: run_room_trigger(zone, id) runs ALL triggers on that room whatever
their flags (self = room). The firetrig command and /api/admin/triggers/fire
also run a body directly.

Also fired: SPEECH_TO (ask/tell/whisper), RANDOM (13 s pulse; GLOBAL lifts the
"zone has players" gate), BRIBE (coins given to a mob; globals value, platinum,
gold, silver, copper; the trigger's num arg is the minimum in copper), HIT_PERCENT
(num arg = HP% threshold), LOOK, GIVE, CAST, LEAVE, ENTRY, DEFEND and object
ATTACK. For RANDOM and HIT_PERCENT the first statement of the body must be the
`if not percent_chance(N) then return true end` gate; the server reads N from it.

NOT fired (no dispatcher): ACT, RESET, TIME, TIMER, AUTO, MEMORY, DOOR. Use wait()
loops started from LOAD, or run_room_trigger, for periodic behaviour.

Full reference (fire order, bindings, API, require, errors):
fierymud-rs/docs/SCRIPTING.md.

Listeners for GREET, SPEECH, COMMAND are things located in the same room that
have triggers (mobs, and items lying on the floor).

Return value: only COMMAND looks at it. "return false" stops the typed
command; anything else lets it continue.$help$,
      min_level = 100,
      category = 'building',
      usage = 'see also: tstat <zone> <id>',
      source_file = 'data/help/trigger-types.md',
      updated_at = now()
    WHERE id = v_id
      AND (keywords, title, content, min_level, category, usage, source_file)
          IS DISTINCT FROM (ARRAY['trigger-types', 'trigger types', 'trigger flags', 'flags']::text[], 'Trigger Types and Variables', $help$Flags a trigger can carry, when the server fires them, and what self / actor /
object are. self is always the entity the trigger is attached to.

Fired by the server today:
  LOAD       mob   Mob spawns (boot and respawn). self = actor = the mob.
                   Not fired for mobs made by room:spawn_mobile.
  GREET      mob   A player or mob arrives in the room. self = listener,
  GREET_ALL        actor = arriver. Both flags behave identically.
  SPEECH     mob   Someone uses "say" in the room, or "ask <mob> <topic>".
                   Global speech = the text, lowercased.
                   Via say, actor is the same entity as self (the speaker is
                   not available). Via ask, actor = the asker.
  RECEIVE    mob   A player gives the mob an item. self = mob, actor = giver,
                   object = the item (the only event that sets object).
  COMMAND    mob   A player types any command while in the same room (mob or
                   item triggers; room triggers are not asked). Globals cmd
                   (command word) and args (rest of line). actor = typist.
                   "return false" consumes the command.
  FIGHT      mob   After each combat round while it is a target. self = target,
                   actor = attacker. Throttle with time.stamp.
  ATTACK     mob   A player starts an attack on it. self = target, actor = attacker.
  DEATH      mob   Just before the mob dies. self = actor = the mob.
  GET, DROP, WEAR, REMOVE, USE, CONSUME   object
                   self = the item, actor = the player. object is nil.
  PREENTRY   room  Before movers enter. self = the room, actor = mover.
  POSTENTRY  room  After the mover arrives and GREET ran. Same bindings.

